nis solved by the points that satisfy the inequalities ![](images/23/23f2bda2195f51e1cbf95f6905d547dc9004733d89866ae9f92ef046c330417c.svg) *and* ![](images/87/877dcbf886336f3054b3df8910cee950868e2819e007cf11544a6be7f15b81d3.svg) simultaneously.\n\nTo find the points that satisfy both inequalities, we first draw the graph of the inequality ![](images/9a/9a758452dbe8e0ede75fb97296110356c18e46275000ac28ebf631d91fa05b22.svg)\n\n![](images/6f/6f3f7b6eb3109225256c5f4342333d03c19ef31b40d5ae5b24c136950a31f76a.png)\n\nNow, on top of the diagram above, we draw the graph of the second inequality, ![](images/c1/c1e37a6573ce7b419aeff619c181b43325304505c05b669394ef0818ace2555f.svg)\n\n![](images/e0/e017eefa235ac4b95009570c59fe5e5587f50bb02299305cfb9126573c0156bd.png)\n\nThe solution to the system is the *intersection* of the two regions (i.e., the part that is shaded twice).\n\n![](images/c1/c1d9b4358e15ca09e8358f8e298fc0ffa745b885adcd7ea522e07f1d221a2c90.png)\n\nThe important thing to realize is that *any* point in the shaded region above satisfies *both* inequalities." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111822 #edb/ref 1065 1473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111822 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1e005009-6033-5e6b-b50c-c802bbffe3e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111822 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115179 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 